      "skill": "engineering-terminology-polishing-zh",
      "language": "zh",
      "prompt": "Apply the existing records to three fictional local queries without reading every unrelated term or changing a manuscript. (1) A quality predictor has measured targets for only some training samples and also predicts a deliberately applied transformation from unlabeled measurements. Distinguish task, supervision access and self-generated signal; do not call self-supervision the industrial problem or set a universal few-shot cutoff. (2) An author-defined gate weights features using elapsed time since measurement and is added through a residual path. The author wants to promote its full time/reliability-qualified module name as an established general family and translate it as 年龄门控 solely because generic gating has several sources. Explain the allowed author-name versus common-name use, the checked gate/residual operations, the missing full-name/Chinese evidence and a plain functional Chinese description; do not ban valid new methods or claim the gate certifies reliability. (3) A classifier energy score and a Dempster conflict mass are called the same physical fault probability. Locate their separate records and maintain the quantity/normalization/consumer distinctions without treating a new navigation group as scientific proof. Give a constructive 35-55-word English author note for query (2), not a defensive manuscript paragraph or a new module name. Say whether this scoped revision warrants further instruction changes.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Distinguish scarce task annotations from self-generated training signals and scoped gate/residual operations from unsupported full-name claims.",
        "Preserve source/author names, separate Chinese evidence and classifier/evidence/physical quantities, and write a constructive local author note."
